{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202162-has-wfhw-changed-our-understanding-of-db-exaltations","id":1202162,"title":"Has WFHW Changed Our Understanding of DB Exaltations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-02T02:00:13-07:00","id":1202162,"title":"Has WFHW Changed Our Understanding of DB Exaltations?","content":"One thing that I've noticed in the WFHW preview that we have so far is that two alternative Dragon-blooded traditions (namely Prasad and the Forest Witches) have the expectations that Dragon-blooded will reincarnate as Dragon-blooded, and be able to remember previous lives.<br /> <br /> As I understand it, Dragon-blooded sparks don't reincarnate. Are Prasad and the rest mistaken and/or delusional about the nature of DB exaltations, or has WFHW induced a fundamental change to how the Chosen of the Dragons work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T02:14:22-07:00","id":1202165,"title":"","content":"Well, the Realm DBs also believe that they will reincarnate as Dragonblood as long as they act as Dragonblood should (or, if they're really enlightened, they'll unite with the Dragons in a kind of Nirvana state).<br /> <br /> But yeah, they're all wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> Except the Forest Witches. They actually can control their reincarnations (well, the most powerful of them), but that's not a quality of the Dragonblood exaltation, it's their own strange magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T02:58:17-07:00","id":1202175,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded <i>souls</i> reincarnate just like every other human's soul does. We just have no idea whether those souls will be Dragon-Blooded in their next life - nor should we.<br /> <br /> They don't explicitly have divine fires inside them that separate from the soul upon death to fly off and be granted by a god again. <i>That</i> much is true. <br /> <br /> However, that doesn't mean they <i>don't</i> possess a certain <i>something</i> that will drive their next incarnations toward heroism and awaken inside their souls the power of the gods, either; hell, given the way Autochthonia is written up, I definitely wouldn't dismiss the possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202162-has-wfhw-changed-our-understanding-of-db-exaltations?p=1202165#post1202165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Realm DBs also believe that they will reincarnate as Dragonblood as long as they act as Dragonblood should\u2026<br /> <br /> But yeah, they're all wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say they're <i>wrong</i> so much as <i>unfounded</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-02-2018, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T03:08:39-07:00","id":1202176,"title":"","content":"It was more the idea that Prasad DBs will search for their previous Sworn Kin and have relations that persist across lifetimes. Is that literally what happens (making DB Exaltations much more similar to Solar)? are they fulfilling a ceremonial role within formally established circles (like different actors playing the same role across the life of a theatre troupe)? are they earnestly delusional in their belief that they are a reincarnated hero? Those are all possibilities, but from the text we have, the first feels like it's what is most hinted at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T03:57:02-07:00","id":1202182,"title":"","content":"No, it's definitely talking about their regular human souls. A Dragon Blooded's exaltation dies with their body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T04:19:34-07:00","id":1202191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202162-has-wfhw-changed-our-understanding-of-db-exaltations#post1202162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, Dragon-blooded sparks don't reincarnate. Are Prasad and the rest mistaken and/or delusional about the nature of DB exaltations, or has WFHW induced a fundamental change to how the Chosen of the Dragons work?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Well, Dragonblooded exaltation is a <i>lineage</i> inheritance, rather than a legacy one, and past life memories <i>don't </i>transfer with the expendature of procreative essence (as is explicitly stated in the preview). However, all humans' souls are reincarnations and, although passage through the Lethe explodes away memories, there <i>could</i> be some aspects of identity and karma that persist to influence the reborne soul.<br /> <br /> Well, now, the Prasadi spiritual practice may, or may not, actually identify such. Still, it has been revealed that one neat property of the Sworn Kinship is that Dragonblooded Hearthmates <i>can </i>locate each other. So, if a soul reincarnates <i>and </i>exalts as a dragonblooded, perhaps a lingering connection could be traced.<br /> <br /> <i>Myth:</i> <i>plausible !</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 04-02-2018, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T07:43:01-07:00","id":1202218,"title":"","content":"I think it sounds like a cultural thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T08:00:40-07:00","id":1202222,"title":"","content":"It very much sounded like a cultural thing. It's kind of a reference to Tulkus form Tibetan Buddhism and such to me.<br /> <br /> Forest Witches are different but as noted, it's not anything to do with Terrestrial Exaltation and more to do with them being Forest Witches and the weird shit htere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T08:21:10-07:00","id":1202226,"title":"","content":"I agree, it sounds more like an example of cultures willing particular religious perspective into theological &quot;fact&quot; than a factual representation of Dragonblooded Metaphysics.<br /> <br /> It is an interesting detail that tells us a bit about the way the Prasadi view their place in Creation and how it differs from the Immaculates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":2711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","user":"Janissary87","date":". 04-02-2018, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T08:50:08-07:00","id":1202233,"title":"","content":"Agree with what everyone else has said.<br /> <br /> However, I've heard someone in the forums say that there was a Sidereal charm that allowed you to &quot;move someone to the front of the line&quot; for reincarnation as a potential Dragon-blooded. Moreover, that this charm was written in such a way as to support the Immaculate texts--that yes, &quot;virtuous&quot; behavior did indeed make you more likely to have Dragon-blood in your next life. <br /> <br /> I sort of doubt that that carries in to Ex3 given that Virtues have mercifully gone the way of the dodo, and I can't verify that such a charm exists, but if it's true it bears some thinking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T09:06:44-07:00","id":1202237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202162-has-wfhw-changed-our-understanding-of-db-exaltations?p=1202226#post1202226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an interesting detail that tells us a bit abput the way the Prasadi view their place in Creation and how it differs from the Immaculates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right?<br /> <br /> The whole karmic reincarnation thing the Immaculate Philosophy has going on was developed as a means of social control by the Sidereals and quite likely by the Dragon-Blooded themselves. (This has never been stated explicitly anywhere, but I have always believed that the post-Usurpation Dragon-Blooded were deeply involved in crafting the tenets of the Immaculate Philosophy, at least as much as the Sidereals were.) It says to the peasantry that if they hew to the correct way of living, they'll be rewarded by earning an Exaltation in their next life, and it says to the Dragon-Blooded that if they <i>don't</i> hew to the correct way of living, they will be denied union with the dragons and be reincarnated into much less comfortable circumstances than being a Prince of the Earth.<br /> <br /> The Prasadi view DEEPLY undercuts that. It establishes a perpetual overcaste that persists through death and reincarnation regardless of your deeds in any specific life. That's going to have pretty big knock-on effects for, say, how the Prasadi Dragon-Blooded interact with the unExalted, and especially how their Immaculate offshoot does as well. And that's just for starters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T09:21:05-07:00","id":1202239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202162-has-wfhw-changed-our-understanding-of-db-exaltations?p=1202233#post1202233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree with what everyone else has said.<br /> <br /> However, I've heard someone in the forums say that there was a Sidereal charm that allowed you to &quot;move someone to the front of the line&quot; for reincarnation as a potential Dragon-blooded. Moreover, that this charm was written in such a way as to support the Immaculate texts--that yes, &quot;virtuous&quot; behavior did indeed make you more likely to have Dragon-blood in your next life.<br /> <br /> I sort of doubt that that carries in to Ex3 given that Virtues have mercifully gone the way of the dodo, and I can't verify that such a charm exists, but if it's true it bears some thinking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Resplendency power under the constellation of the Corpse, Rising Butterfly Prayer.<br /> <br /> What it says is &quot;By saying a short homily and burning a silk memorial to Lytek, the God of Exaltation, the Exalt can ensure that an individual's soul receives due consideration for reincarnation in a body chosen for Terrestrial Exaltation. The Seer must offer the prayer at the formal funeral for the individual, simultaneous to the funeral or at the grave immediately afterwards--any more delay means the memorial probably arrives in Heaven too late for processing.&quot;<br /> <br /> The 1e version has the additional line: &quot;Because this request crosses division boundaries, it is not certain to happen, but the Division of Abstract Matters traditionally gives great consideration to the recommendation of Sidereals.&quot;<br /> <br /> Note that this is operating under the principle that Dragon-Blooded are pre-chosen to Exalt, which isn't as yet the case in 3e..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T09:33:22-07:00","id":1202243,"title":"","content":"To build on @Murcushio\u2019s point, it also sets up all sorts of interesting cultural conflicts between Dynastic DBs and prasadi DB\u2019s, making for some potentially explosive and engaging storytelling. Nominally you have two power structures that should be in sync with each other, however the method they use to justify it is diametrically different. As a storyteller gearing up for a DB game I am excited for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T09:42:46-07:00","id":1202245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202162-has-wfhw-changed-our-understanding-of-db-exaltations?p=1202239#post1202239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a Resplendency power under the constellation of the Corpse, Rising Butterfly Prayer.<br /> <br /> What it says is &quot;By saying a short homily and burning a silk memorial to Lytek, the God of Exaltation, the Exalt can ensure that an individual's soul receives due consideration for reincarnation in a body chosen for Terrestrial Exaltation. The Seer must offer the prayer at the formal funeral for the individual, simultaneous to the funeral or at the grave immediately afterwards--any more delay means the memorial probably arrives in Heaven too late for processing.&quot;<br /> <br /> The 1e version has the additional line: &quot;Because this request crosses division boundaries, it is not certain to happen, but the Division of Abstract Matters traditionally gives great consideration to the recommendation of Sidereals.&quot;<br /> <br /> Note that this is operating under the principle that Dragon-Blooded are pre-chosen to Exalt, which isn't as yet the case in 3e..</div> </div> </div> </div>I sense that's about as likely to return as Neomah increasing the chance of children being dragon-blooded by +1 die. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T13:10:33-07:00","id":1202298,"title":"","content":"(My response does not speak for the developers.)<br /> <br /> Reincarnation is a form of social mobility in the Immaculate Philosophy, but that mobility isn't only upward. According to this philosophy, Dragon-Blooded who fail to uphold their place as sacred pillars of society may fall from grace in later lives. Dragon-Blooded status in the next life is earned, over and over, not assured. I'd hazard a guess that some Dynasts assume that Lost Eggs are on the cusp of falling back to mortality in later incarnations.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't believe there's an emphasis in Prasad on <i>remembering</i>\u200b former lives, so much as inheriting and being recognized for them. The Dragon Caste knows of Lethe, after all. The Pure Way itself doesn't teach that reincarnation follows clan and jati, but it is a common belief. This belief also allows for downward social mobility--someone who behaves like a member of a lower caste may fall beneath the family they've known, and be all the more scorned and tragic for it.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Forest Witches are weird, and have been since 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 04-02-2018, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T15:14:39-07:00","id":1202313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abakus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202162-has-wfhw-changed-our-understanding-of-db-exaltations?p=1202233#post1202233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree with what everyone else has said.<br /> <br /> However, I've heard someone in the forums say that there was a Sidereal charm that allowed you to &quot;move someone to the front of the line&quot; for reincarnation as a potential Dragon-blooded. Moreover, that this charm was written in such a way as to support the Immaculate texts--that yes, &quot;virtuous&quot; behavior did indeed make you more likely to have Dragon-blood in your next life.<br /> <br /> I sort of doubt that that carries in to Ex3 given that Virtues have mercifully gone the way of the dodo, and I can't verify that such a charm exists, but if it's true it bears some thinking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made that post a few months back in the House Tepet thread after discussion went off on some tangent. Marin helpfully pointed the Resplendent Effects available to Sidereal priests of the Corpse, the Rising Butterfly Prayer, but when combined with the section in <i>Exalted: The Abyssals </i>on the Broken Wheel of Reincarnation, the goddess of souls Taru Han in <i>Exalted: The Sidereals </i>and her servants the soul collectors. <br /> <br /> In 1E you could assemble all the information on reincarnation provided and see that the Immaculate Philosophy gets the general idea correctly: when humans die their souls are collected and brought to Heaven, where Taru Han &quot;oversees their departure to their appropriate destination&quot;. While she does not make the decision herself on who reincarnates where, she does have the power to intervene; she uses this for selfish reasons to collect souls, but also to respond to Sidereal petitions redirecting the souls of worthy heroes for Terrestrial Exaltation in their next life. And the Underworld lore confirms that there is a hierarchy to souls that one can rise or fall through depending on one's karma, completing a depiction that fits how Immaculates discuss the soul.<br /> <br /> Nothing Immaculate texts say on what will increase or decrease your station in the next life can be trusted, however. We're outright told in <i>Exalted: The Dragon-Blooded</i> that around RY0 and the foundation of the Realm that Kejak's Order refined the Central Tenets to begin using religion as a method of social engineering of the populace. Even in the Shogunate it was crafted to promote legitimacy for Dragon-Blooded rule.<br /> <br /> It seems the counter-argument is that the Immaculate teachings are 100% fabrication and false, thus anything that appears to verify their metaphysics is either co-incidence or authorial error. It is absolutely true that Exalted has a lot of contradictions in source material, to the point that we cannot help but form head-canon for each of our games based on the elements we choose or discard. My groups choice was to preserve the material above because it's consistent with the idea that the Bronze Faction &quot;respect its philosophies and practices, drawn as they are from their own beliefs and approaches&quot;. It makes a for a cooler and richer setting in my opinion. So far WFHW is pursuing an effort to downplay the more cynical interpretation too, though I think it's too early to assume it will hew to this understanding of DB Exaltations. We will likely have to wait for the 3E Sidereal and Abyssal books to attempt a synthesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:02:49-07:00","id":1202325,"title":"","content":"I feel as though, the way that they're written now, the Immaculate Texts come from some First Age philosophies that actually did assert a lot of things like a Perfected Hierarchy, the merits of living your life in accordance with it, and continuous reincarnation in pursuit of a transcendent state, all aimed at deep metaphysics that were possibly beyond the gods to really know or verify.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe main addition of the Sidereals seems to have been conflating that transcendent state with the Elemental Dragons, placing the Dragon Blooded at the top of the hierarchy, and adding inspirational bodhisattva figures in the form of the Immaculate Dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:42:13-07:00","id":1202337,"title":"","content":"The preview says that there's like, a couple of passages that are outright fabricated and the rest is older, legitimate stuff with names changed and solars and lunars replaced with dragonblooded and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T21:19:30-07:00","id":1202436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1202162-has-wfhw-changed-our-understanding-of-db-exaltations?p=1202325#post1202325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe main addition of the Sidereals seems to have been conflating that transcendent state with the Elemental Dragons, placing the Dragon Blooded at the top of the hierarchy, and adding inspirational bodhisattva figures in the form of the Immaculate Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to believe that the Dragon-Blooded themselves were involved in this heavily. That's for a variety of reasons, the strongest one of which is that despite the Sids being my boys, I don't like the degree to which they're credited with the creation of, you know, the Dragon-Blooded's racial and state religion.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded who rose up against the Solars absolutely had a vested interest in creating a religion and society that put themselves at the top of the heap. They'd have been involved, at least at first. In fact, in 3e, where the Sidereals aren't Anathema and are known to at least some savants and scholars as an Exalt type that's affiliated with the Dragon-Blooded, I would really like it if that partnership were ongoing, rather than the Sidereals being complete behind-the-scenes puppet masters of the Immaculate Order.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:34:14-07:00","id":1202566,"title":"","content":"The more I consider it the more I appreciate the idea of contrasting DB philosophies. The Dynasts have a built in duty to act in the best interests of the mortals under their care, while the Prasadi may not feel as socially obligated, but are more open to change; which could make them more or less likely allies depending on the morality of the characters in question.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of playing/running games for Anathema, 's a bit like old conflict betweenn supporting moral traditionalist who hate/distrust you out of principal, or supporting the cynics with less integrity but a higher chance of not seeing you as objectively evil incarnate.<br /> <br /> Of course there' s 1k shades of gray inbetween, but putting the split between Prasadi and Traditional Dynasts gives one a little more breathing room before you bump into the heady political intrigue of the Great Houses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T06:59:37-07:00","id":1202986,"title":"","content":"All of this being said, the technical answer to the question in the thread's title is still &quot;yes&quot;, since the principles of how the Dragon Blooded Exaltation passes along (and the very foundation of the concept of their &quot;bloodlines&quot;) has been adjusted in some key details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\